<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>sh.paseo.desktop.launcher</string>
	<!--
	  Starts the Paseo DESKTOP app at login so this host is always reachable as a
	  Paseo execution target from the phone / latios / any other client.

	  Installed on ALL Macs in the fleet (kinto, latios, nimbus). Not hostname-gated:
	  Paseo's model is one daemon per execution host, and clients pick which host owns
	  the work. Kinto is the one that matters most (always-on, the host Rai drives
	  from his phone), but a daemon on each is the documented topology.

	  REPLACES sh.paseo.daemon (removed 2026-07-27). That agent ran a HEADLESS
	  `paseo daemon start --foreground`, which cannot coexist with the desktop app:
	  Paseo.app spawns its own "Paseo Supervisor" -> daemon pair and binds
	  127.0.0.1:6767 the moment it launches, so the headless agent always lost the
	  port. Observed on kinto: 101 crash-loop restarts against KeepAlive, each exiting
	  1 with "Another Paseo daemon is already running (PID 16427)". Every doomed
	  attempt still touched the outbound relay before dying, flapping the relay route
	  and making Paseo on the phone unresponsive -- precisely the remote-control
	  failure the agent existed to prevent. See logs/paseo.md.

	  So the desktop app now owns the daemon, and we solve the thing the headless
	  agent was genuinely good at -- environment -- in ~/bin/paseo-desktop instead.
	  That wrapper sources ~/.config/zsh/*.zsh (the chezmoi-managed 1Password secret
	  groups) and then execs the app bundle, so the app, the Supervisor, the daemon
	  and every agent CLI beneath them inherit one correct environment by ordinary
	  process inheritance. Full rationale lives in the wrapper's header comment.

	  Paseo.app ALSO performs its own login-shell env capture (`/bin/zsh -i -l -c`,
	  30s timeout) when it spawns a daemon. The wrapper is deliberately belt-and-
	  braces: that capture is best-effort and can time out under load, whereas
	  sourcing the groups directly cannot.

	  KeepAlive is deliberately FALSE, unlike the old headless agent. This launches a
	  GUI app; if Rai quits Paseo he means it, and KeepAlive would resurrect it on
	  every quit. RunAtLoad covers the only case that matters (reboot).

	  Secrets stay out of this plist deliberately: it lands in ~/Library/LaunchAgents
	  at mode 644. launchd supplies only the two vars below; the wrapper builds the
	  rest. We also deliberately avoid `launchctl setenv`, which would expose all ~82
	  credentials to every GUI app in the session via `launchctl getenv`.

	  SECURITY POSTURE (deliberate, do not widen without Rai's say-so):
	    * Daemon listens on 127.0.0.1:6767 only. No inbound port on any host.
	    * Remote access is via Paseo's outbound relay (E2E encrypted; the relay sees
	      connection metadata, never prompts, code, or responses).
	    * Therefore the PAIRING LINK is the sole trust anchor -- treat it exactly like
	      a password. `paseo daemon pair` prints it; never paste it anywhere.
	    * To go relay-free instead, bind to the tailnet IP and add --no-relay. That is
	      a bigger exposure decision on a work machine and is Rai's call, not a
	      default.
	-->
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/bin/paseo-desktop</string>
	</array>
	<key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
	<dict>
		<key>HOME</key>
		<string>{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}</string>
		<key>PATH</key>
		<string>{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/bin:{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/bin:{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/Library/pnpm:{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.bun/bin:{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.asdf/shims:{{ if eq .chezmoi.arch "arm64" }}/opt/homebrew/bin:/opt/homebrew/sbin{{ else }}/usr/local/bin:/usr/local/sbin{{ end }}:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
	</dict>
	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<false/>
	<key>StandardOutPath</key>
	<string>{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/Library/Logs/paseo-desktop.log</string>
	<key>StandardErrorPath</key>
	<string>{{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/Library/Logs/paseo-desktop.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
